{"base":"92981bf2909d564fc94631fa95c8d1eb4dbe1ed4","description":"- route `seed`/`unseed` through `announce()` so the radiroh:// location\n  they write (or retract) reaches peers, instead of leaving it local\n- honor `--no-sync` to defer the announce, matching register and the\n  other mutating commands\n- thread `no_sync` through `node run`/`seed`/`unseed` so both the\n  top-level aliases and the `node` subcommands behave the same\n\nPreviously seed signed a location into the COB but never announced it,\nso in a script ending after seeding the location silently never reached\nthe network unless the user remembered `rad sync -a`.\n\n\nfeat(cli): add `register --seed` to register and seed in one step\n\n- add a `--seed` flag to `register` that, after writing the artifact\n  entry, hands the bytes to the local node and announces a radiroh://\n  location — equivalent to a follow-up `seed`, but in one command\n- extract `seed_to_release` so register reuses the CID it already\n  computed instead of re-hashing the file in the seed path; large\n  artifacts are now hashed once instead of twice\n- have `register_artifact` return the resolved release id and CID so the\n  caller can drive the seed and announce once for both COB writes\n\nCollapses the canonical two-command, two-hash publish flow (`register`\nthen `seed`) into a single invocation, mirroring the existing\n`fetch --seed`.\n\n\nfeat(cli): add `--json` to register\n\n- add a `--json` flag to `register` that emits\n  `{cid, release_id, revision}` on stdout in place of the human summary\n- skip the stderr summary and discovery hints in JSON mode so stdout is\n  a single clean object, even alongside `--seed`\n\nMutating commands had no machine-readable output, so a script needing\nthe resulting release id or CID had to re-derive the CID or scrape\nstderr. This makes the register step composable in pipelines.","oid":"2e4d47c9fd38dfed8c99f13535f8199c513f4918","type":"revision"}